.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-CREATE-NAMESPACE 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-create-namespace \- create a new namespace under an account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam create-namespace
.BR \-\-account\-id | \-a
.I ACCOUNTID
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
[\fB\-\-description\fR|\fB\-d\fR \fIDESCRIPTION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a new namespace under an account (e.g. \fIdevelopment\fR,
\fIintegration\fR, \fIproduction\fR) via the eam service's
.I create-namespace
action.
.PP
The caller must be a global administrator, or hold account-scoped
administrator privileges on \fIACCOUNTID\fR (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-grant-namespace-access (1)
for how an account-scoped administrator grant is created).
.PP
The account identified by \fIACCOUNTID\fR must already exist (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-account (1)).
Namespace names only need to be unique within their account - two
different accounts may each have their own \fIproduction\fR namespace.
.PP
The created namespace's JSON representation is printed to standard
output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-account\-id " " \fIACCOUNTID\fR
Account the namespace belongs to. Required.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Namespace name, unique within \fIACCOUNTID\fR. Required.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-description " " \fIDESCRIPTION\fR
Free-text description of the namespace's purpose. Defaults to an empty
string.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The namespace was created.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, the caller
lacks administrator privileges on the account, the account does not
exist, or a namespace with that name already exists under the account. If
the failure was an expired or invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the
stored credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam create-namespace \e
    --account-id 123456789012 --name production \e
    --description "Production workloads"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
